==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[coterminous]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|conterminus|lang=la}} from {{term|con-||with|lang=la}} + {{term|terminus||border, end|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/kɒnˈtɜː.mɪ.nəs/|/kənˈtɜː.mɪ.nəs/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/kənˈtɝ.mɪ.nəs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-conterminous.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Meeting [[end-to-end]] or at the ends.
# {{context|of geographical regions}} [[adjoin|Adjoining]]; sharing a [[boundary]].
#:''New York's borough of Brooklyn and Kings County are '''conterminous'''.''
#:''To get a building warrant he had to show the plans to "'''conterminous''' proprietors", neighbours with whom his property shared a boundary.''
# Having the same [[scope]], [[range]] of meaning, or [[extent]] in time.
# (of property leases) linked or related and expiring together.

